    <description>ALF-RS-04 FR10 (per-item): fires when an AppraisalItem&apos;s own AF_ApprovalStatus__c changes to Approved. Notifies the initiating rep + customer Contact that THIS SPECIFIC VEHICLE was approved, referencing the item (AppraisalItemNumber / Make-Model-Year), mirroring AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved&apos;s dual-recipient emailSimple + Custom Notification pattern exactly. Deliberately does NOT reassign Appraisal.OwnerId here - that reassignment already happens correctly at the Appraisal level, driven by AF_FL_AppraisalItem_RollupApprovalToAppraisal writing Appraisal.AF_ApprovalStatus__c, which re-triggers the EXISTING AF_FL_Appraisal_ApprovalApproved flow (owner reassignment + its own rep/Contact email) once ALL items on the Appraisal are Approved. This flow&apos;s own email is the finer-grained &quot;your vehicle was approved&quot; notice per item, separate from and complementary to that final Appraisal-level &quot;the whole trade-in is approved&quot; notice - duplicating owner reassignment here would be redundant and could race the rollup flow&apos;s own field update in the same transaction. AppraisalItem has no direct Contact/InitiatingSalesRep relationship fields of its own (confirmed via describe), so Get_Appraisal hops via AppraisalId to read AF_Contact__c/AF_InitiatingSalesRep__c off the parent.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&apos;&lt;html&gt;&lt;body style=&quot;margin:0;padding:16px;background-color:#F4F4F6;font-family:Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif;&quot;&gt;&lt;div style=&quot;max-width:560px;margin:0 auto;background:#FFFFFF;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid #E2E5EA;border-top:4px solid #0B2545;padding:20px 24px;&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 style=&quot;margin:0 0 12px;font-size:18px;color:#0B2545;&quot;&gt;Trade-In Vehicle Approved&lt;/h2&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0 0 6px;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;The trade-in valuation for vehicle &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalItemNumber} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt; (Appraisal &lt;strong&gt;&apos; &amp; {!Get_Appraisal.AppraisalNumber} &amp; &apos;&lt;/strong&gt;) was approved.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;margin:0;font-size:14px;color:#4A4A4A;&quot;&gt;Once every vehicle on this trade-in is approved, the overall Appraisal will move to Approved and be handed back to you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/body&gt;&lt;/html&gt;&apos;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>EmailSubject</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Approved: Trade-In Vehicle &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalItemNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>Formula_RecipientEmails</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>IF(
    ISBLANK({!Get_Contact.Email}),
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email},
    {!Get_Rep_ForEmail.Email} &amp; &quot;,&quot; &amp; {!Get_Contact.Email}
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifBody</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;The trade-in valuation for vehicle &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalItemNumber} &amp; &quot; was approved.&quot;</expression>
    </formulas>
    <formulas>
        <name>NotifTitle</name>
        <dataType>String</dataType>
        <expression>&quot;Trade-In Vehicle Approved: &quot; &amp; {!$Record.AppraisalItemNumber}</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Appraisal Item Approval Approved {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Appraisal Item Approval Approved</label>
